{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:20:31Z","created_by_operation":"op_6cfce975fbc04bc18cf36a381084f0f0","id":"pg_e3c964a6fa95541c8a90e0c5447d3cfb","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/momozi1996-momo-code-use-restrictions-md-6922581961d5-e0c5447d3cfb.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_9f91296f936f5c62837e05a4646dbe72"],"title":"momozi1996/momo-code/USE_RESTRICTIONS.md @ 6922581961d5","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:20:31Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6cfce975fbc04bc18cf36a381084f0f0"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:20:31Z","created_by_operation":"op_6cfce975fbc04bc18cf36a381084f0f0","id":"pg_fa7217da349d5b46894b93f17334574b","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/momozi1996-momo-code-user-guide-md-6922581961d5-93f17334574b.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_aa8e16b8d4565ecb90f46e22d1b3300c"],"title":"momozi1996/momo-code/USER_GUIDE.md @ 6922581961d5","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:20:31Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6cfce975fbc04bc18cf36a381084f0f0"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_03f6ee3cb3216d76e21e79fc386b899aab1ca17a9e25b3f6fd38c04e9683e26d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The /agent command decomposes tasks into child momo subagent processes run in parallel with a synthesizer merging results, bounded by env rails MOMO_RLM_MAX_DEPTH (3), MOMO_RLM_BUDGET (8), and MOMO_RLM_TIMEOUT_MS (300000)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_0f0c61c13a67061253c8049431529122170ac90bd9c359da43e9e28855347741"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README describes an experience fast loop (/evolve) using a KEP protocol: observe session signals, distill tactics, select via Thompson sampling, inject into prompts, solidify stats, and promote high-confidence tactics to the fine-tune curriculum."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1d0be991eb85aa51a36239d001c41c71a81a197c4511d1c57bd6eb1dbb22ef8c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product includes task-level evaluation features: `momo /sim eval --tasks=tasks.json` runs batch evaluation with a fresh world per episode, and /optim studies score configurations via a --cmd metric from stdout or --sim Genesis experiments."},{"claim_ids":["clm_636ce741eaae905a70798e6da1a77b051d314c48352098915229985fd20889f5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A `momo serve` command exposes a local HTTP JSON API plus SSE live feed and a single-file dashboard, defaulting to 127.0.0.1:4097; non-loopback binding requires a --token with Bearer auth."},{"claim_ids":["clm_86e5a6dd80f74dae7c8ca679ff663df4840dc84dcd5efc102fb1c83e226d054c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"On first run the tool creates ~/.momo/ containing config (momo.jsonc), sessions, and experience/ with tactics records and a ledger.jsonl audit log; graph state persists to ~/.momo/graphs/<id>.json after each batch so runs survive restarts."},{"claim_ids":["clm_91557e6776df095f30d2ba63f69d540eabbc4d9ae4ed754f66a2cf179929f204"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A weight slow loop (/fine-tune) is documented to improve model weights at hour-level timescales via signal mining, curriculum synthesis, Monte Carlo Graph Search, LoRA fine-tuning, and a ratchet gate for monotonic improvement."},{"claim_ids":["clm_92117918843caf4b21cc6b602294bdffba998d8c2afd2ab0ad3a592403079fdf"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Model tiers ultra/standard/lite are selectable via --model with documented use cases (complex tasks, daily coding, quick low-latency tasks), and a `momo models` subcommand lists models, model info, and providers."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ecf49c6fe076b578689ec5bef16e653457d1d0f10ecbcef0a3c208bdec4cf70b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The /refine command reviews session trajectories and proposes tactic or prompt-patch improvements, and nothing is applied without explicit human approval via approve/apply review-gate subcommands."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f7255d40d6ab206af355d2742af583fe5f591c86b70533defbd9722e61445080"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The /graph command plans a directed acyclic graph of subagent tasks, runs nodes in parallel per topological level with retries and downstream dependency outputs, supports resume/status/list, and can mark nodes as simulation agents driving the Genesis world via /sim."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f99b53b80156215ccaf5821524acac143920045a548ff550f4055c14fefc51fe"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Runtime prerequisites are macOS or Linux (Windows via WSL), Node.js >= 20, git, and curl; the /sim feature additionally requires Python with genesis-world installed, and /voice requires sounddevice and scipy plus an OpenAI-compatible speech-to-text endpoint."}],"claim_ids":["clm_03f6ee3cb3216d76e21e79fc386b899aab1ca17a9e25b3f6fd38c04e9683e26d","clm_0f0c61c13a67061253c8049431529122170ac90bd9c359da43e9e28855347741","clm_1d0be991eb85aa51a36239d001c41c71a81a197c4511d1c57bd6eb1dbb22ef8c","clm_636ce741eaae905a70798e6da1a77b051d314c48352098915229985fd20889f5","clm_86e5a6dd80f74dae7c8ca679ff663df4840dc84dcd5efc102fb1c83e226d054c","clm_91557e6776df095f30d2ba63f69d540eabbc4d9ae4ed754f66a2cf179929f204","clm_92117918843caf4b21cc6b602294bdffba998d8c2afd2ab0ad3a592403079fdf","clm_ecf49c6fe076b578689ec5bef16e653457d1d0f10ecbcef0a3c208bdec4cf70b","clm_f7255d40d6ab206af355d2742af583fe5f591c86b70533defbd9722e61445080","clm_f99b53b80156215ccaf5821524acac143920045a548ff550f4055c14fefc51fe"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:20:31Z","created_by_operation":"op_6cfce975fbc04bc18cf36a381084f0f0","id":"pg_fbdea5ade5735a6aa029375046f9210c","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/momozi1996-momo-code-readme-md-6922581961d5-375046f9210c.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_75fc6f2327e651638ffb3f0d40ef31e4"],"title":"momozi1996/momo-code/README.md @ 6922581961d5","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:20:31Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6cfce975fbc04bc18cf36a381084f0f0"}
